  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">AD LECTOREM.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">
      <i>HABES Lector quæ de Crucè</i>
    </l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>scripsimus, sed germana.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Antea atque alibi quæ edita</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>(credas hoc nobis) non sunt nostra.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Quid ergo? non illa dictavimus?</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Fortasse. sed o imperitiam! quasi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>edendi illo fine. Reverentior posteritatis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>sum: &amp; aliud scio esse Sche-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>dia, aliud Opera; nec subitaria</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>hæc nostra dedicanda in Memoriæ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>templo. Quid, quòd alii graviùs</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>etiam peccant? qui excipiunt aut</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>intercipiunt dicta aut oratiunculas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>nostras, &amp; in contumeliam mei</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>divulgant. Aliter non accipio.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Ævum hoc ut multis deliciis fibu-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>lam, ita petulantiæ &amp; licentiæ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>laxat: &amp; quod avet procacissimus</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The initial H of HABES is a large woodcut-style letter; it is printed as one initial with "ABES" in small capitals. The line "* 3" is the signature and "quis-" the catchword. Italic/roman distinctions in the body are approximate. Some words in the lower-left corner are damaged by stains and not legible.</notes>
